WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.049
SOC 2 is not solely the responsibility of security or compliance teams.

2
00:00:05.049 --> 00:00:13.929
A SOC 2 report reflects how the organization operates, which means many employees contribute to control performance and evidence quality.

3
00:00:13.929 --> 00:00:27.708
Employees support SOC 2 by following policies, protecting information, using approved systems, completing training, documenting work, reporting concerns, and respecting access control processes.

4
00:00:27.708 --> 00:00:41.048
Engineers and developers may contribute through secure development practices, code review, change management, logging, monitoring, vulnerability remediation, and incident response participation.

5
00:00:41.048 --> 00:00:52.392
Managers may contribute by approving access, reviewing responsibilities, ensuring training completion, supporting remediation work, and reinforcing expectations within their teams.

6
00:00:52.392 --> 00:01:02.170
HR, finance, legal, IT, security, operations, and customer-facing teams may all own or support controls depending on the scope.

7
00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:08.067
The exact responsibilities vary by organization, but the shared theme is consistent operation.

8
00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:09.554
Small behaviors matter.

9
00:01:09.554 --> 00:01:21.557
Using a ticket instead of an informal message, recording an approval, closing a review, escalating an issue, or completing training on time can all support evidence and accountability.

10
00:01:21.557 --> 00:01:25.958
A strong SOC 2 culture makes control performance part of normal work.

11
00:01:25.958 --> 00:01:33.052
People understand why the process exists, what record needs to be kept, and who to contact when something does not look right.

12
00:01:33.052 --> 00:01:37.233
This does not mean every employee needs to become a compliance specialist.

13
00:01:37.233 --> 00:01:44.836
It means each person should understand the controls connected to their role and treat process documentation as part of doing the job well.
